@chapter 19 | Food Chemistry, Fertilizers and Chemistry Miscellany

@intro
The last chemistry chapter covers **food preservation** (sodium benzoate, nitrogen packing, refrigeration), **sugars** (honey, invert sugar), **fertilisers** (urea, ammonium sulphate, DAP), and a long miscellany of **chemicals in daily life**: insecticides and rat poisons, cloud seeding, dyes and inks, glass, batteries, matches, soil amendments, chemical weapons and smoke screens. It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 19.1 | Food Preservation

@q 30:1-4

@table
Method | How it works
**Sodium benzoate / benzoic acid** | Most common chemical **preservative** for fruit juices, squashes, sauces (FSSAI limits apply)
Potassium metabisulphite | Preserves colourless foods (lime juice, white wine)
Salt, sugar, vinegar | Draw water out of microbes (osmosis), lower pH (pickles, jams)
**Nitrogen flushing** | Chips packets are filled with **inert nitrogen**, which stops **oxidation** (rancidity) and cushions the chips
**Refrigeration** | **Slows** the growth of microbes and the rate of biochemical (enzyme) reactions; does not kill germs
Pasteurisation, canning, irradiation | Kill microbes by heat or gamma rays
@end

@q 30:5

**Animal charcoal** (bone char) is used to **decolourise** cane sugar during refining; activated charcoal adsorbs colouring matter.

@section 19.2 | Sugars and Foods

@q 30:6

@src 30:7
@pyq U.P. P.C.S. (Pre) 2020
Given below are two statements, one is labelled as Assertion (A) and other as Reason (R) :
Assertion (A) : Invert sugar is more sweet than sucrose.
Reason (R) : Invert sugar is obtained by the hydrolysis of sucrose.
Select the correct answer from the code given below:
Code :
(a) Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).
(b) Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A).
(c) (A) is true but (R) is false.
(d) (A) is false but (R) is true.
@ans (b)
@end

**Honey** is mostly **fructose (about 38%)** and glucose (about 31%), with about 17% water. **Invert sugar** is a 1:1 mixture of glucose and fructose made by splitting (hydrolysing) sucrose; it is sweeter because **fructose is the sweetest natural sugar**. Its sweetness comes from the fructose, not from the way it is made, so (R) does not explain (A).

@q 30:11-12

**Jelly** needs fruit rich in **pectin** and acid: guava, apple, plum and citrus are best. **Organic food** is grown without synthetic fertilisers and pesticides; **Sikkim** became India's first fully organic state (2016).

@section 19.3 | Chemicals in Medicine and Daily Use

@q 30:8-10

**Carbon monoxide** binds haemoglobin about 200-250 times more strongly than oxygen, forming **carboxyhaemoglobin**, so even small amounts suffocate (deaths from charcoal heaters in closed rooms). **Eugenol** gives clove oil its smell and numbs toothache.

@q 30:13

Detergents clean because they **lower** the surface tension of water, letting it wet and lift grease; one end of a detergent molecule binds oil and the other binds water.

