@q 32:24-26

@src1 32:2
@one
Which of the following main substances (elements) is used in making matches?
@ans Phosphorus
@end

**Safety matches**: **red phosphorus** on the striking strip, potassium chlorate and antimony sulphide on the match head. **White phosphorus** glows in the dark (**phosphorescence**, really chemiluminescence), catches fire in air and is stored under water. A car battery is a **lead-acid** accumulator with **sulphuric acid**; a dry cell uses **manganese dioxide**, zinc and carbon.

