@trap
**Sodium benzoate** preserves fruit juice. Chips bags hold **nitrogen**, not air. Refrigeration **slows**, not kills. **Honey = mostly fructose**. **Urea is organic, 46% N, amide form; DAP = 18-46.** **Ammonium sulphate** acidifies soil most. **Gypsum** reclaims alkaline soil. **Silver iodide → artificial rain**, **eosin → red ink**, **zinc phosphide → rat poison**, **zinc oxide → philosopher's wool**. **Crookes glass cuts UV.** **Red phosphorus** in safety matches. A dry cell **cannot** be recharged. Car batteries use **sulphuric acid**.
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
These are long-running, highly repeated **use-of-chemical** questions, often as four-pair matches (2013, 2019, 2020). Fertiliser numbers (urea's nitrogen, DAP's ratio) and food chemistry (invert sugar, honey) are favourites of the Mains and recent Prelims papers.
@end

